<title>CHILE: Chile January supermarket sales rise sharply.</title>
<headline>Chile January supermarket sales rise sharply.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean supermarket sales climbed 15.7 percent in January against the same month last year, said the National Statistics Institute.</p>
<p>The figures showed sales in January falling 23 percent compared with levels reported in December.</p>
<p>The institute calculates the sales figures from a survey of 555 stores with more than three cash tills throughout Chile.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
